00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:26.920
I am going to talk for a minute about the
fact that the new PubMed Labs is a truly responsive

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:33.290
site. This means the features you see on the
desktop will also be available on your mobile

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:41.720
device. Now, this development has to be optimized
for mobile device be sure when you build your

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:45.620
responsive design and when you think about
how it's going to act on to act on a mobile

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:50.649
device, you don't want it to override any
native phone features that are really handy

00:13:50.649 --> 00:13:54.399
or make it more cumbersome that it needs to
be. There is a lot of design that is gone

00:13:54.399 --> 00:14:00.120
into this responsive piece because there's
a lot of information on these PubMed screens.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:04.540
How to present that information on a mobile
design is quite a challenge.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:09.470
I listed here a few of the features that are
available on mobile right now. You can log

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:17.660
into your my NCBI account. The advanced search
is available. We have filters and the timeline.

